WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-How are you?

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:01.768 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm good.

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.069
I just left a city full of
people dressed like that.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, everybody in Washington
is very happy.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's been --
When was the last time

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
a Washington sports team
won a title?

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it, like,
early '90s or something?

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.244 size:84% position:42%
-I can't even remember.
-It's been a long time.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.312 line:92%
So, that's the -- I'm glad --

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.146 line:92%
-I don't root for any of 'em.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You don't watch --
you know, you're a --

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:15.715 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I'm a Philadelphia fan.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you probably,
more often than not,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
actively work against them,
right?

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do everything I can
to sabotage them.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:22.455 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I want to talk about
the book.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.025 size:78% position:39% line:92%
But first, obviously,

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:27.560
you managed to do this while you
still have your day job.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.331
And yesterday -- Often on
Sunday, you are the first

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:35.635
to catch what would be called --
I guess politely be called spin.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Spin.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Larry Kudlow,
the chief economic advisor,

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.939 size:78% position:39%
he came on your show
and he basically said

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.208
Justin Trudeau stabbed
Donald Trump in the back.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:45.945
And the worst part about it was
that he weakened Donald Trump

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
before his summit
with Kim Jong-un.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:49.315 line:92%
What is it like to watch that

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
take form in real time
on your show?

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:54.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's just fascinating
because, obviously,

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
we all saw the G7 blow up
the way it did.

00:00:57.424 --> 00:01:01.561
And President Trump on Air Force
One firing off his tweets,

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:05.932
removing the United States
from a -- from a communiqué.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-As one does.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:07.901 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there really hadn't been
any explanation

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:11.504 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
about why it was.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so Larry Kudlow
came on the show.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I didn't know
what they were gonna say.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:18.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
I legitimate --
Usually, you have an idea

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.446 line:92%
of what they're going to say.

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:21.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this was
the birth of the spin.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:23.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, obviously,
it was coordinated

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:27.487
because they were saying it at
the same time on other channels

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.188 size:81% position:41% line:92%
with different guests.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:32.459
But the birth of the spin, that
this was Justin Trudeau's fault.

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:32.892 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it so offended
Donald Trump.

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then, do you --
in those times,

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you're processing in
real time,

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.767
do you find, like, it's your job
to give them room

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
to lay this out
for everyone to see?

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:46.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I mean, part of the job
is these are your leaders.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-What are they saying?

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:51.244
And then my job is to push back
and challenge it.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:54.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
For instance -- I don't know
if you guys knew.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.617
But on occasion, President Trump
has been known --

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.051 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:01.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-On occasion
to insult people too.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:03.823 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Breaking news.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You really have to follow
the news closely.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause he does it
between the lines.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's very subtle.
-It's subtle. It's subtle.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
The occasional bon mot.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:17.770 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously there has been
a lot talking --

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.908
We just showed a clip.
He doesn't feel like preparation

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that important
for this meeting.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:24.477 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No. It's instinct.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:26.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you feel like his national
security advisers

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:27.480 size:78% position:39% line:92%
are panicked by this?

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.649
Or do you think, at this point,
they would be shocked

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
if he said, "Let's bone up
on North Korea"?

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think that
they would be shocked.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:36.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, he's not -- he's never
been a detail guy.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:37.390 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.726
-I think that
the national security team there

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:42.228 size:81% position:41% line:92%
is smart and prepared.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do wonder about
this initial meeting

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:45.765 line:92%
that they're going to have

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:48.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
where it's just Kim Jong-un
and President Trump

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
and two translators
and that's it.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:51.804 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause usually it's not done
that way.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:56.209 size:84% position:42%
And no one really knows
what's going to happen.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:59.512
And afterwards, no one will
really know what happened.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:02:59.979 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:04.851
Because no one from that room
can be, like, trusted, right?

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In the terms of a novel,
where you --

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:11.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have four
unreliable narrators.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We do have four un--
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:14.561 line:92%
Now, Donald Trump doesn't --

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:17.497
you know, it seems like in times
that he's talked about

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:18.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
our nuclear arsenal
and our plan,

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:22.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
he doesn't seem to understand
the finer details of it.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:22.669 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, that's right.

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:25.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a debate in 2015
when Hugh Hewitt,

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
the conservative
talk-radio host,

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:29.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
asked him about
the nuclear triad.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:30.677 line:92%
And the nuclear triad is --

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:34.280
you know, it's having nukes from
land, from sea, and from air.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was pretty clear
he had no idea

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:37.850 line:92%
what the nuclear triad is.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
What's amazing about
this stuff --

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
now, obviously,
he's in charge of it.

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:42.655 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:45.725 line:92%
-Is the idea that there is no,

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:48.695
"Oh, I didn't know that.
I need to bone up on it."

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:49.128 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.164
There's no shame in not knowing
things and boning up.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:51.931 line:92%
-No. No. A million things.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it always happens during
any presidential race.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:57.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
All candidates get caught not
knowing things.

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:58.238 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But for instance,
he has this thing.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.474 line:92%
He just did it the other day.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:04.510
You know, NATO,
this -- this alliance we're in.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.580
The deal was, the commitment
was, every country in NATO

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:12.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
has agreed to spend 2% of
their GDP on defense spending.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
Kind of a wonky thing,
but that's an important thing.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
President Trump portrays it
as, you know,

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:17.657 line:92%
they're not paying their dues.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
None of these other countries
are paying their dues.

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:22.862
Now, he has an argument to make
about these other countries

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.397 line:92%
need to carry their weight more.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.399 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But it's not dues.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not a country club.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:33.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not, you know,
$200,000 are owed

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:34.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then you get
the greens fees.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:38.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
"They're not signing
for their club sandwiches."

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I don't understand.
-Yeah.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know --
Have people tried to explain?

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:42.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
I assume people
have tried to explain.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:46.152
-Well, then, the other question
is, we don't, you know, every --

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:47.153 line:92%
We, obviously, have a sense of

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:48.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
what he knows about
our nuclear arsenal.

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is no one really --
Is Kim Jong-un an expert

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:53.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
on nuclear arsenal,
or is he gonna be too --

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:54.060 line:92%
is he very similar to Trump?

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.696
Is it gonna be two guys sitting
in a room talking about --

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:58.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We know so little about him.
-Yeah.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Honestly, it's so opaque
that North Korea --

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:01.801 line:92%
there's so little that the --

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:04.904
that U.S. intelligence knows
about what he knows, et cetera.

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:08.207
As you noted, he won't even let
people study his stool.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:11.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's how --
-I mean, that's --

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:15.148
So, if we don't even know that,
how do you think -- I mean.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:15.581 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Exactly.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
There must be a real story
in that stool for you

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
to bring your own toilet.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.187 line:92%
-So they still have corn.

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:23.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.224 size:75% position:38% line:92%
That's good to know.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:28.194
-I'm just thinking as an --
-Yeah. Thinking out loud.

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:30.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As an intelligence officer
might.

